## The Same-Source Serre Buffer

The explicit q79 degree-two K3 already contains the rational branch point

```text
p_* = [x:y:z:w] = [1:-1:1:0].
```

At `(1,-1,1)`, both `Q2` and `G3` vanish. Moreover `H4=3`, so

```text
grad(F6) = H4 grad(Q2) = (3,6,3) != 0.
```

Thus `p_*` is a smooth point of the locked K3 and is the same point used in
the Hartshorne-Serre qutrit construction.

There is a unique nonzero extension up to isomorphism

```text
0 -> O_K3 -> E_- -> I_(p_*)(-H) -> 0.             (1)
```

Indeed, the degree-two polarization gives

```text
