E18 = C3_sigma tensor E6.
```

Then `E18` is locally free and

```text
ch(E18) = 18-3H.
```

No continuous choice is introduced: the point is fixed by the locked q79
equation, the extension space is one-dimensional, and all nonzero extension
classes are isomorphic after scalar automorphisms.

## Zero-Section Correction

Let `i0:D0->J` be the regular zero-section embedding. Its normal line is
trivial because `J=K3 x E*`. Grothendieck-Riemann-Roch gives

```text
Ch_alpha(i0_*E18)
  = i0_*(ch(E18) td(N_i0)^(-1))
  = 18D0 - 3H*D0.                                  (2)
```

The normalized gerbe makes (2) an alpha-twisted object canonically. The
rigidified degree-zero Poincare lines restrict trivially at `p0`, so the
standard qutrit matrices on `C3_sigma` give the same sigma-projective
categorical action as on `S_ind`.

